{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe current reconciler has typed `MutationDirection` and `MutationAction`, but `Mutation.payload` remains `Mapping[str, Any]`. Outbound typed mutations are translated back into the legacy batch dictionary, two CREATE shapes coexist, and string/monkeypatch consumers make deletion non-local. ADR 0103 already owns retry, coordinator, and observe-before-replay policy; this story must not redesign those decisions.\n\nThis is the architecture prerequisite for the typed cutover. It completes RESEARCH and any required ADR lifecycle before dependent implementation begins.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Enumerate every valid `(direction, action)` pair, producer, consumer, serialization/manifest field, compatibility re-export, string import, standalone-loaded test module, and transport boundary. Use semantic references plus string search.\n- Define the smallest discriminated payload union that makes invalid field/action combinations unrepresentable while preserving necessary provenance and canonical comparison.\n- Decide ownership of payload validation, canonical serialization, adapter projection, follow-ons/suppression, binding identity, and provider-neutral outcomes.\n- Treat producer-construction inputs as part of the contract: inventory the current 24-value `_compute_outbound_update_mutation` seam and its 14/11-value field-diff collaborators; decide how observation, transport/runtime, mapping policy, diagnostics, and output construction flow through cohesive existing domain owners. Reject a wrapper that merely repackages the same loose bundle or introduces a second generic pass/ticket context.\n- Specify expand/compare/cut/delete sequencing, rollback, and exact legacy deletion targets. Production dual-send is forbidden.\n- Reconcile the design with ADRs 0004, 0026–0029, 0083, 0092, and 0103. If a new structural decision is required, complete the architecture-decision RESEARCH -> critique -> DRAFT -> HOLD -> MERGE lifecycle before closing this story.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` — mutation producers, planners, coordinator, adapters, manifests, and compatibility surfaces.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` — consumer census and existing contract evidence.\n- `docs/adr/` — one atomic decision record only if accepted ADRs do not already decide the representation boundary.\n\n## Testing\n\nThis story produces architecture evidence rather than production behavior. Verify the consumer census with both Serena semantic references and repository text search; verify the direction/action matrix against the enum allowlist and every planner/adapter route; run plan review on the resulting implementation stories after the ADR disposition is settled.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A checked-in or ticket-recorded census covers every mutation producer/consumer and all string, dynamic-load, monkeypatch, manifest, and transport consumers; an empty semantic result is confirmed by text search. — Delivered in ADR 0107 §\"Census\" (Serena `find_referencing_symbols`/`find_symbol` across `mutation.py`, `outbound_mutation_builders.py`, `outbound_differ.py`, `batch_dispatch.py`, `applier.py`, `apply_base.py`, `typed_dispatch.py`, `apply_inbound.py`, `apply_outbound.py`, `differ.py`, `observation.py`, `ticket_plan.py`, `outbound_field_diff.py`, reconciled against `grep` for string/monkeypatch/dynamic-load sites); confirms `(inbound, delete)` and `(inbound, probe)` are enum-valid but dead (no producer, no `_LEAVES` handler; removed by bug 3b5f per `apply_inbound.py`'s own docstring).\n- [x] Every valid direction/action pair has a named payload contract with required/optional fields and validation rules; no proposed contract relies on one option-heavy generic action payload. — ADR 0107 §\"Discriminated payload union\" defines all 10 live `(direction, action)` payload types with required/optional field tables and validation-ownership assignment; explicitly rejects a single generic payload.\n- [x] The design states which current canonical bytes/hashes are compatibility requirements and which normalized representation is comparison-only. — ADR 0107 §\"Canonical bytes vs. comparison-only representation\" distinguishes the serialized-manifest compatibility surface from the shadow/live comparison's normalized view.\n- [x] Retry/idempotency/fuse ownership remains with ADR 0103's coordinator; no adapter or payload type introduces a second retry owner. — ADR 0107 explicitly reaffirms ADR 0103 as sole retry/idempotency/fuse owner; no payload type is assigned retry responsibility.\n- [x] Shadow comparison is side-effect-free, and live comparison uses isolated Jira targets/instances rather than dual-sending to one issue. — ADR 0107 §\"Migration sequencing\" states this explicitly and forbids production dual-send.\n- [x] The migration has explicit entry/exit criteria and names `_mutation_to_batch_dict`, legacy batch dispatch, duplicate CREATE handling, obsolete re-exports, and compatibility tests as deletion targets. — ADR 0107 §\"Migration sequencing\" (expand/compare/cut/delete) names each of these as explicit deletion targets with entry/exit criteria per phase.\n- [x] The design explicitly dispositions the current 24/14/11-value producer seams and names the cohesive input boundaries the implementation will use; it does not merely wrap the same values or duplicate `Observation`, `TicketPlan`, or the current pass/runtime owner. — ADR 0107 §\"Producer-seam disposition\" assigns the 23/14/11-parameter seams to four existing owners (`OutboundDiffConfig`, `Observation`/`TicketPlan`, Backend-port collaborators, observability sinks); explicitly rejects a new generic context object.\n- [x] Any required ADR is merged with explicit approval before dependent code work; otherwise the evidence records why accepted ADRs already decide the shape. — No accepted ADR already decides the `Mutation.payload` representation boundary (0004/0026-0029/0083/0092/0103 reconciled and found silent on this boundary), so ADR 0107 was authored. It is recorded as **Proposed (DRAFT)**, not Accepted: an autonomous agent session cannot self-certify a MERGE per the architecture-decision RESEARCH->DRAFT->HOLD->MERGE lifecycle's explicit-authorization requirement. The ADR itself states, and this ticket's closing comment states, that the dependent implementation story (`earthborn-statuelike-boutu`) must not begin until a human operator moves ADR 0107 to Accepted — this is the evidence recording why the gate is open, satisfying this AC's \"otherwise\" branch honestly rather than fabricating an approval."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788058795033238001,"uuid":"53027a43-1fdf-4f8b-ac32-3e470605e368"}